- It was a wig!

00:08:44.615 --> 00:08:45.682
It was a lot!

00:08:45.682 --> 00:08:47.430
They did a lot to me.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.340
It was teeth, it was wig, it was nose.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.834
- [Kelly] No, but what
I'm saying, though -

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:53.010
- [Sofia] Plastic from here to here!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.407
- [Kelly] But what I'm
saying is, it looks like,

00:08:54.407 --> 00:08:57.330
no, how I'm saying is
they did such a good job

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.230
that it looked seamless

00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:59.310
and you just looked like a different,

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.680
like you literally look
like you could actually

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.150
just be this person in other movies.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.050
You could have two careers.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:04.883
- [Sofia] See?

00:09:04.883 --> 00:09:05.730
Like, she looks real, right?

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:06.563
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:09:06.563 --> 00:09:07.396
- [Sofia] I know.

00:09:07.396 --> 00:09:09.351
- You look like you're
a different actress,

00:09:09.351 --> 00:09:11.730
like you could have a
whole different life.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.400
- That's exactly what I
wanted, that reaction.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.640
And I love that you thought
that it was just a little thing.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.164
- [Kelly] Because they did a good job!

00:09:19.164 --> 00:09:19.997
- Because that means it's natural.

00:09:19.997 --> 00:09:20.925
- [Kelly] Exactly, that's what I'm saying.

00:09:20.925 --> 00:09:23.610
I love, too, that we just
get to see you in that role.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:24.630
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.190
This is such a departure
from Modern Family,

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.180
such a departure from things.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.560
You know, even on America's Got Talent,

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.150
your personality in general, like,

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:34.080
it's such a cool departure
and such a cool flex for you.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.000
Like a cool muscle to be
able to flex for everybody.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.700
- Well, you know, I was always worried

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.590
when I decided to do it,

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.876
I'm like, I just don't want to think,

00:09:42.876 --> 00:09:46.386
I wanted Sofia and Gloria
Pritchett to disappear.

00:09:46.386 --> 00:09:48.306
I didn't want the audience to say,

00:09:48.306 --> 00:09:51.300
why does Gloria Pritchett think
that with that rubber nose,

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:55.050
she can, you know, trick us
into that she's a dramatic,

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.720
you know, killer actress, you know?

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:58.843
- It happens, you are.

00:09:58.843 --> 00:10:01.080
- But I was worried the whole time.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:05.160
I was like, are they gonna see
Gloria Pritchett in Griselda?

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.180
I mean -
- [Kelly] No.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.013
- Did you see it?

00:10:07.013 --> 00:10:09.510
- You don't see you at
all in this character.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:10.802
It's like insane.

00:10:10.802 --> 00:10:11.635
(laughs)

00:10:11.635 --> 00:10:13.110
I just remember going,
wait, what happened?

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:13.943
What did they do?

00:10:13.943 --> 00:10:14.776
I don't understand.

00:10:14.776 --> 00:10:16.689
Even your voice is different.

00:10:16.689 --> 00:10:20.880
- The way I walked, I had
to learn how to smoke,

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.480
I had to learn, I don't
know if I can say that here,

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.627
to do cocaine, but-

00:10:25.627 --> 00:10:26.460
- Yeah.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.620
- But not real cocaine, of course.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.588
Fake cocaine, like, a thing.

00:10:30.588 --> 00:10:33.840
But I was 50 years old
and I had never even

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:36.572
touched a cigarette, so I
had to learn how to hold it.

00:10:36.572 --> 00:10:37.874
- Yeah.
(applause)

00:10:37.874 --> 00:10:40.770
- That was stressing me, because you know,

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:42.600
people that have been
smoking their whole life,

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.655
they're like -
- It's so innate.

00:10:43.655 --> 00:10:46.590
- It's an extension of their arm.

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.303
And I was at the beginning like:

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:50.727
- Well if you were doing this,

00:10:50.727 --> 00:10:52.284
then you're used to smoking something.

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:56.400
(applause)
(laughter)

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:57.270
I'm just messing with you.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.250
All right, let's take another break.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.440
Griselda premieres tomorrow on Netflix.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.990
Y'all have got to check it out.

